From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] skw: name the TX dynamic workqueue per-CPU

Mainline requires WQ_PERCPU or WQ_UNBOUND and warns otherwise. Per-CPU is
what the queue already was, and what a queue without either flag is before
6.17 named it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/swt6621s_wifi/skw_tx.c b/drivers/swt6621s_wifi/skw_tx.c
index d196d62..b8ecaa6 100644
--- a/drivers/swt6621s_wifi/skw_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/swt6621s_wifi/skw_tx.c
@@ -1429,7 +1429,11 @@ static int __skw_tx_init(struct skw_core *skw)
 		return -EFAULT;
 	}
 
+	/* per-CPU, the default before 6.17 named it */
 	skw->tx_dy = alloc_workqueue("skwifid_dywq.%d",
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 17, 0)
+			WQ_PERCPU |
+#endif
 			WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_SYSFS,
 			0, skw->idx);
 	if (!skw->tx_dy) {
